    {
      "path": "/paths/~1v1~1check-input",
      "added": {
        "post": {
          "summary": "Check Input Photo",
          "description": "**What does this photo show?** (blueprint B19, tool `route_medication_image`): loose pills, a blister pack, a box or\nbottle, printed text or a document, and which tools fit it. The user's own word comes first; otherwise the photo's\ndescription is checked (a net, not a guarantee: ask the user when `type` is `unchecked`). PDFs are documents: send\nthem to `/v1/read-label` directly.",
          "operationId": "check_input_photo_v1_check_input_post",
          "requestBody": {
            "content": {
              "multipart/form-data": {
                "schema": {
                  "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Body_check_input_photo_v1_check_input_post"
                }
              }
            },
            "required": true
          },
          "responses": {
            "200": {
              "description": "Successful Response",
              "content": {
                "application/json": {
                  "schema": {
                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/CheckInputResponse"
                  }
                }
              }
            },
            "401": {
              "description": "unauthorised",
              "content": {
                "application/json": {
                  "schema": {
                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                  }
                }
              }
            },
            "404": {
              "description": "not_found",
              "content": {
                "application/json": {
                  "schema": {
                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                  }
                }
              }
            },
            "409": {
              "description": "version_mismatch",
              "content": {
                "application/json": {
                  "schema": {
                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                  }
                }
              }
            },
            "422": {
              "description": "invalid_input",
              "content": {
                "application/json": {
                  "schema": {
                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                  }
                }
              }
            },
            "500": {
              "description": "model_error",
              "content": {
                "application/json": {
                  "schema": {
                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                  }
                }
              }
            },
            "502": {
              "description": "upstream_failed",
              "content": {
                "application/json": {
                  "schema": {
                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                  }
                }
              }
            },
            "503": {
              "description": "not_ready",
              "content": {
                "application/json": {
                  "schema": {
                    "$ref": "#/components/schemas/Error"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "path": "/paths/~1v1~1feedback~1{consent_id}/delete/description",
      "before": "Withdrawal of consent: deletes every photo stored under this consent id.",
      "after": "Withdrawal of consent: deletes every photo stored under this consent id, here and in the dataset repo, squashes\nthe repo's history, and checks before saying `deleted` (blueprint B15). Safe to repeat."
    },
    {
      "path": "/paths/~1v1~1model-info/get/description",
      "before": "The served model (blueprint B3): service version vs model version, the embedding space and preprocessing that\nstored embeddings must match, the calibrated decision rule, and what the model was trained on and where it is weak.",
      "after": "The served model (blueprint B3, B25): service version vs model version, the embedding space and preprocessing that\nstored embeddings must match, the calibrated decision rule, what the model was trained on and where it is weak,\nhow similarity is computed, and the measured error rates with the evaluation file each comes from."
    },
    {
      "path": "/paths/~1v1~1read-label/post/description",
      "before": "**Which medicine is on this box, label or prescription?** Reads the printed text and finds the medicine names in\nit (RxNorm's ingredient and brand names, international names such as paracetamol too), with strength,\ningredients, RxNorm code, and what is printed about each (directions, quantity, dose form, dates), every value\nwith the line it was read from and `null` when not printed (blueprint B7). With `medications`, each medicine is\ncompared with the patient's list: same medicine, different strength, or not on the list (B9). Send a confirmed\ncandidate to `/v1/safety/medications` as `{\"id\", \"name\", \"rxcui\"}`. Always ask the user to confirm.\nNothing is stored; only the lines that name or describe a medicine are returned (labels show the patient's name).",
      "after": "**What does the pharmacy sticker say?** Made for Singapore dispensing labels (the sticker on the medicine bag or\nbox), also reads prescriptions and manufacturer boxes. Per medicine: name, strength per unit, ingredients and\nRxNorm code; the quantity supplied (amount and unit); the instructions parsed into dose, times a day or every N\nhours, as needed, time of day, before/after food, duration and daily maximum; what it is for; cautions; dispensing\nand expiry dates. Every value comes with the line it was read from and is `null` when not printed, never inferred\n(blueprint B7). `label_kind` says whether it is a dispensing label (instructions for the patient) or a package.\nWith `medications`, each medicine is compared with the patient's list: same medicine, different strength, or not\non the list (B9). Send a confirmed\ncandidate to `/v1/safety/medications` as `{\"id\", \"name\", \"rxcui\"}`. Always ask the user to confirm.\nNothing is stored; only the lines that name or describe a medicine are returned (labels show the patient's name)."
    },
    {
